1
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,480
Staff Officer Liang,

2
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,680
here are the documents you needed printed.

3
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:37,680
Thanks.

4
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:40,560
I've been printing for an hour and a half.

5
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,280
The printer is practically smoking.

6
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:44,480
Appreciate it.

7
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:45,640
You've heard, right?

8
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:46,960
About Guo Zijian leaving the service.

9
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:58,760
This guy...

10
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,240
how should I put it?

11
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,320
It's a shame.

12
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:04,680
Yeah.

13
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:05,920
Yeah.

14
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,080
It's a shame.

15
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:09,840
Staff Officer Liang.

16
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:12,160
You hate to see him go too.

17
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,720
It's not that I'll miss him.

18
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,600
I just think...

19
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,800
for someone who can bring our directing work

20
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,040
problems,

21
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:22,840
or even tough challenges, to leave just like that...

22
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:25,080
For our research work,

23
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,080
it's a huge loss.

24
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,400
Fair enough.

25
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,880
But this Guo Zijian...

26
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:33,040
he really doesn't play by the rules.

27
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:34,320
I mean,

28
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,640
a stack of scoring criteria this thick

29
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,120
still can't rein in a wild horse like him.

30
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:43,880
Yeah.

31
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,280
Guo Zijian is a

32
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,840
wild horse who doesn't understand rules.

33
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,960
So the rules don't like him either.

34
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,240
Staff Officer Liang, where are you going?

35
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,720
I'm going out for some fresh air.

36
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,280
Didn't I say no send-offs?

37
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,800
I changed my mind, okay?

38
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:24,640
Lin Yihu and those brats...

39
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,160
They usually stick to you like glue.

40
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:28,040
But look at today.

41
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,800
They're nowhere to be seen.

42
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,440
Isn't it better if they don't?

43
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,040
Seeing off a defeated

44
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,360
and disgraced battalion commander...

45
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,000
It's embarrassing for everyone.

46
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,680
What's embarrassing about it?

47
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:46,120
We're seeing off our own battalion commander.

48
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:47,600
It's not embarrassing at all.

49
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,560
Does it have to be this sentimental?

50
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:58,760
Commander.

51
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:01,040
We don't want you to leave.

52
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:03,560
Lin Yihu!

53
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:04,520
Here!

54
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,600
Why aren't you at the hospital with Wu Dongsheng?

55
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,400
Why are you causing trouble here?

56
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,320
Don't worry, sir.

57
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,520
I've arranged everything for the squad leader.

58
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:15,680
But you...

59
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,079
you can't leave.

60
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:18,440
If you leave,

61
00:04:18,839 --> 00:04:20,120
what will happen to the 1st Battalion?

62
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:22,079
What about us, your comrades?

63
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:24,560
What do you mean?

64
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:28,800
The 1st Battalion belongs to the People's Liberation Army.

65
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,120
It doesn't belong to me, Guo Zijian.

66
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:35,640
Li Songwei!

67
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:37,760
As a company commander,

68
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,040
why are you joining the ruckus?

69
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:41,360
If a company commander's direct superior

70
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:42,520
turns into a deserter,

71
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,120
then what is the point

72
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,840
of being a company commander?

73
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,280
This isn't deserting.

74
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:53,440
I'm changing battlefields.

75
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,560
The 1st Battalion is your battlefield!

76
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:58,160
Li Songwei!

77
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,960
You've got some nerve,

78
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,320
talking to me like that.

79
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:05,520
If you go back to being our battalion commander,

80
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:08,200
I'll always speak to you respectfully.

81
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:25,560
Li Songwei

82
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,560
Here!

83
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:27,360
Dong Zhenguo

84
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:28,040
Here!

85
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:28,720
Sun Xingwang

86
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:29,280
Here!

87
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:32,240
Let me ask you one thing.

88
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,280
Am I still your battalion commander?

89
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,560
Yes, sir!

90
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,440
Do my orders still stand?

91
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,640
They do, sir!

92
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,160
Since you acknowledge me as your commander,

93
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:44,720
follow my orders.

94
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,920
Break formation!

95
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:57,120
Disperse!

96
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,760
If anything happens with Wu Dongsheng,

97
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:28,120
let me know immediately.

98
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:58,880
Battalion Commander

99
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:02,800
Battalion Commander

100
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,040
Battalion Commander

101
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,400
Is anyone here?

102
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:42,280
Boss, I'll have a bowl of noodles.

103
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:43,720
Coming right up!

104
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,480
Freeze! We're the police!

105
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,720
Help! They're fake cops!

106
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:07,920
They're fake cops!

107
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:10,360
Help! Help!

108
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:13,920
Police business!

109
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,480
Don't panic, everyone!

110
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,200
What's going on?

111
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:24,680
We're from the Criminal Investigation Division.

112
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:27,440
We're from the Haitong Police Department.

113
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:29,320
We contacted Captain Han earlier.

114
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:31,200
We're here on a cross-jurisdictional manhunt.

115
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:32,559
Ah, you're one of us.

116
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:33,320
Welcome, welcome.

117
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:35,039
Let's head back to the precinct first, then.

118
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,159
Daqiang.

119
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,000
Take him

120
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,000
away.

121
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:38,440
Yes, sir.

122
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,080
Officer.

123
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,520
Let me see your badge again.

124
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:58,840
Sure.

125
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:03,640
Get down!

126
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:05,120
Let them all go!

127
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:06,440
Or I'll kill her!

128
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:07,600
Step back!

129
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,400
Hurry up!

130
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,160
Step back!

131
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,720
I told you to step back!

132
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:30,600
Alright.

133
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:31,960
Thank you for your cooperation.

134
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:32,840
Thanks.

135
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:34,560
Got everything cleared up?

136
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:35,880
Yes, it's all clear.

137
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,080
You can go now.

138
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:45,000
How did you know

139
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,600
I was in the Special Forces?

140
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,840
From the way you took down the first guy,

141
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:49,880
I could tell.

142
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:52,920
I heard you're leaving the army.

143
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:54,720
Do you want to come to Haitong?

144
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,120
Our Criminal Investigation Team

145
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,880
would love to have someone with your talents.

146
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:00,400
To be your assistant?

147
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,640
If you're willing,

148
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,120
I'll give up my captain position to you.

149
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,640
That doesn't sound too bad.

150
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:09,440
Give it some serious thought.

151
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:11,280
If you don't have a girlfriend,

152
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,040
I can help with that too,

153
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:15,600
so you can settle down in Haitong.

154
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:16,840
What?

155
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:18,680
To repay me for saving your life,

156
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:19,840
are you offering yourself to me?

157
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,080
I wouldn't rule it out.

158
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,280
I think I'll pass.

159
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,360
A female captain who hunts scammers

160
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:30,600
but gets tricked by them herself...

161
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:31,720
is too much for me to handle.

162
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:35,320
You're right.

163
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:36,120
My fault.

164
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:38,160
Goodbye.

165
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,640
Just look at the two of you.

166
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:47,440
The older one acts like a kid.

167
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:50,000
And the younger one never grows up.

168
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:53,560
You play this staring contest whenever you meet.

169
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,640
You've been playing it for over a decade.

170
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,440
Don't interrupt.

171
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,680
Grandma, I'm about to win.

172
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,600
In your dreams!

173
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:02,360
Look, look, look!

174
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:02,920
He's about to lose.

175
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:03,920
He's going to blink.

176
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:09,800
Let's eat, let's eat.

177
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,880
Battalion Commander Guo, no cheating.

178
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:14,840
By the way,

179
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,440
about you coming back on leave,

180
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,640
did you tell your dad?

181
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,440
What's there to talk about with him?

182
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,320
I don't mean to nag, Xiaojian,

183
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,320
but you always butt heads with your dad.

184
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:28,880
How many years has it been now?

185
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,200
I just don't understand.

186
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:34,480
How can a father and son hold such grudges?

187
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:35,800
Grandma,

188
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,600
can we talk about something else?

189
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,280
Fine.

190
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:40,520
Let's talk about something else.

191
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,120
Grandpa,

192
00:11:42,880 --> 00:11:44,160
coming back this time,

193
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:46,280
I have a favor to ask you.

194
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,680
I knew something was up.

195
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,280
What trouble did you get into?

196
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:51,480
It's not that.

197
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:54,000
I have a comrade

198
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,760
who had an accident during the exercise.

199
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:58,080
He had an amputation.

200
00:11:59,200 --> 00:11:59,920
I asked around.

201
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:02,800
Doesn't our provincial hospital install those

202
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,160
smart prosthetics?

203
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:06,120
Once installed, he'll be like a normal person

204
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:07,000
and it won't hold him back at all.

205
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:08,920
Could you help me ask about it?

206
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,200
Why ask your grandpa about this?

207
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:15,400
Doesn't your Aunt Qi work at the provincial hospital's

208
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,200
rehabilitation department?

209
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,640
If you ask her, it's a sure thing.

210
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,200
I don't want to beg their family.

211
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,320
What do you mean, "their family"?

212
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:25,920
Your Aunt Qi

213
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:27,400
married your dad,

214
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:29,160
so she's our family now.

215
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:30,920
Xiaojian,

216
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:34,400
your Aunt Qi treats you really well.

217
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,800
If you can't bring yourself to ask her,

218
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,600
I'll ask her for you.

219
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,920
No, no, no, Grandma.

220
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:42,480
I'll call her myself. I'll do it.

221
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:43,920
Come on, let's eat, let's eat.

222
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:44,440
Come on, here you go.

223
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:47,800
For terrain with two facing mountains,

224
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:49,560
although it's advantageous for defense,

225
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:50,920
it's obviously not easy to launch an attack.

226
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,000
First, visibility is limited.

227
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,760
Second, the flanking route is too long.

228
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:56,520
Third, it's easy to get surrounded.

229
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:59,160
The Blue Force command's decoy target

230
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:01,120
was set up in this exact environment.

231
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:02,720
But later,

232
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,600
it was seen through by your Battalion Commander Guo Zijian.

233
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,840
This morning's after-action review

234
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:14,960
will end here for now.

235
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:15,960
This afternoon,

236
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,840
we will use your battalion's

237
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:18,960
success and failure in two battle cases

238
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:20,320
to conduct targeted discussions.

239
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:21,200
Meeting adjourned.

240
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:35,720
Dr. Liang.

241
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,520
Instructor Sang.

242
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:40,920
This...

243
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,920
This is our Battalion Commander Guo Zijian's

244
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:45,200
after-action report on this exercise.

245
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:47,520
I hope you can take a look when you have time.

246
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:50,320
This...

247
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:52,200
shouldn't it be submitted to the brigade headquarters?

248
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,400
Why are you giving it to me?

249
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:54,280
Right.

250
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:56,480
Our battalion commander didn't want to submit it.

251
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,320
He almost tore it up.

252
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,160
I snatched it away from him.

253
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,120
You were the director of this exercise,

254
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:05,200
and an expert.

255
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,920
I hope this report

256
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,040
will be of more value in your hands.

257
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:10,840
Of course,

258
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:14,320
I do have some selfish motives.

259
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,440
I think if this report

260
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,680
can also earn

261
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:19,200
some positive feedback from you,

262
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:21,280
it might have a positive impact

263
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:23,440
on Guo Zijian's future.

264
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,120
This report...

265
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:33,080
will it really have that big of an impact?

266
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:35,160
As for what specific impact it'll have,

267
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,600
I don't know either.

268
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,320
As a grassroots officer,

269
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,120
this is the only resource

270
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:42,680
I have on hand.

271
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:48,040
Okay, I understand.

272
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:49,600
I'll leave it to you then.

273
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:19,960
Xiaoshan.

274
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:21,880
Bro.

275
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:23,200
Are you going to make it back

276
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,720
for my graduation ceremony?

277
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:30,640
Where are you?

278
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:32,280
I knew it!

279
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,000
You wouldn't miss my graduation.

280
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,080
You're the absolute best!

281
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:37,120
My brother is the best brother in the world!

282
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,480
Alright, alright. Save the flattery.

283
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:41,240
What are your plans after graduation?

284
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:42,640
I want to start my own business.

285
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:43,960
Are you sure?

286
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:45,960
Starting a business isn't that simple.

287
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:47,800
I've thought it through.

288
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,160
I'll leverage Dad's Junmeng Group

289
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:52,640
to build a military goods trading platform.

290
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,560
But Dad also gave me a condition.

291
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:56,680
He wants me

292
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,600
to take charge of the R&D department as well.

293
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:02,600
But researching new equipment like drones

294
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:04,320
isn't exactly my strong suit.

295
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:06,880
Bro,

296
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:08,520
why don't you leave the service?

297
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:09,520
Come work with me.

298
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:11,240
We'll see.

299
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:13,040
Don't say "we'll see."

300
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:16,200
You didn't want to go to military school and serve either.

301
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:18,360
You were reluctant,

302
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:21,320
but Dad still forced you down this path.

303
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:26,320
Do you still resent Dad

304
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,360
for changing your college applications back then?

305
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:33,960
Now's your chance to correct that mistake.

306
00:16:34,680 --> 00:16:35,760
Seize the opportunity,

307
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:36,440
Boss Guo.

308
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,840
We siblings can join forces

309
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,800
and run this trading platform together.

310
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:42,520
We'll talk about this later.

311
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:43,600
I'm here for something else.

312
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:44,960
What is it?

313
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:48,200
Could you tell Aunt Qi

314
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:51,040
that I want to consult her about something tomorrow?

315
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:52,320
Sure, no problem.

316
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:53,760
But I'm warning you,

317
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,840
make sure Chen Hanxiao doesn't find out.

318
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:57,680
Of course. We're on the same team.

319
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,720
Why would I let him know?

320
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,440
Professor.

321
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:32,640
I'm sorry to bother you so late,

322
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:35,240
but I have something here

323
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:36,320
that you really need to see.

324
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:50,960
Sit down.

325
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:58,280
Xiaoshan told you, right?

326
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:00,280
Why didn't you come home when you got back?

327
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,920
Your grandparents are so old.

328
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,040
Stop bothering them all the time.

329
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:08,040
To me, that's my real home.

330
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:14,600
How long will you stay this time?

331
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,240
Who knows?

332
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,920
Maybe I'll just stay.

333
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:22,080
Can you just talk to me nicely?

334
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:23,880
You're a soldier.

335
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:25,960
What kind of attitude is this?

336
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:30,600
If you're just here to scold me,

337
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,640
then I won't entertain you.

338
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:32,840
Stop right there!

339
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:39,080
Why were you looking for Aunt Qi?

340
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:41,400
Are you sick or injured?

341
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:42,520
It's none of your business.

342
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:44,960
What do you mean you might not leave?

343
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:48,240
Exactly what you think it means.

344
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:51,840
You want to be a deserter?

345
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:54,280
I never wanted to be a soldier in the first place.

346
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:55,560
Whoever wants to do it can do it.

347
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:56,800
What did you say?

348
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,360
Say that again.

349
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:00,360
I said,

350
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:02,480
I don't want to be a soldier.

351
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:04,440
Whoever wants to do it can do it.

352
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:07,760
Come back here!

353
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:10,280
Come back!

354
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:12,600
Zijian!

355
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:14,840
Wait a moment.

356
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:19,320
What are you two fighting about now?

357
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,280
Wu Dongsheng

358
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:27,120
was severely injured and disabled.

359
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:28,560
As the battalion commander,

360
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,080
you cannot escape the blame.

361
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:33,280
Starting tomorrow, you are suspended from duty.

362
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,000
You will go on leave

363
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:35,920
and await the final decision.

364
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:40,400
Things haven't really reached the worst-case scenario.

365
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,360
You cannot choose a time like this

366
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,200
to talk about giving up.

367
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:47,440
You want to be a deserter?

368
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:53,760
Listen to what he just said!

369
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,520
That's the military!

370
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:56,800
Does he think he can just leave whenever he wants?

371
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:59,800
Do you know how much it costs the country to train a soldier?

372
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,160
Calm down first.

373
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,800
We still haven't figured out what exactly happened, right?

374
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:03,920
What is there to figure out?

375
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:06,280
He was just transferred to a field unit,

376
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:08,080
and he's afraid of the hardship and fatigue!

377
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:10,560
My brother is nothing like that!

378
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,680
Back then, you secretly changed his college preferences

379
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:13,840
to force him into a military academy.

380
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:16,600
He's been doing great in the military all these years.

381
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:18,960
He was always a top student at the academy.

382
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,640
Now he's even a battalion commander.

383
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:22,000
What's so great about being a battalion commander?

384
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:25,000
I was younger than him when I became one!

385
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:27,600
If you ask me,

386
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,360
getting discharged and coming home wouldn't be bad.

387
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:30,920
He could even help you out at the company.

388
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:31,880
Join what company?

389
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:33,160
My company doesn't want him!

390
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:35,720
What is my company called? It's called Junmeng.

391
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,200
Our Junmeng

392
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:40,080
is a large enterprise with defense cooperation credentials!

393
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:41,880
Would we ever hire a deserter like him?

394
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,000
Let me tell you, if he dares to be a deserter,

395
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:45,280
I'll break his legs!

396
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:46,680
Can you even beat him in a fight?

397
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:49,640
Don't jump to conclusions.

398
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:51,800
I just feel like there's another reason behind this.

399
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:54,000
Since he was a child, Zijian

400
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:55,160
has always been incredibly resilient.

401
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:57,320
And he's done well in the military these past few years.

402
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:58,240
Right.

403
00:20:58,240 --> 00:20:59,280
If he suddenly wants to get discharged,

404
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:00,880
could something have happened to him?

405
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,320
You don't need to make excuses for him.

406
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:03,760
I'm making myself perfectly clear today:

407
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,320
if he becomes a deserter,

408
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:07,080
I will disown him.

409
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,720
I'll just pretend I never had this son!

410
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,000
I've finished reading it.

411
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:35,160
Tell me your thoughts first.

412
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:36,640
I think

413
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:38,680
we shouldn't let Comrade Guo Zijian leave the military.

414
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:40,680
It would be a loss for the military.

415
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,480
You think that highly of him?

416
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:45,640
Is it?

417
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:48,200
I'd say it's just being objective.

418
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:50,400
As far as I know,

419
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:52,720
he's set quite a few traps for you.

420
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:53,560
What,

421
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:55,000
you don't hold a grudge?

422
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,280
From a personal perspective,

423
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:59,000
some of his actions did make me

424
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,240
extremely angry.

425
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:04,360
But from the military's perspective,

426
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:06,880
his ideas and concepts are very advanced.

427
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:08,040
Sir,

428
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:10,240
I believe the things he is pursuing

429
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:12,040
and the concepts you always discuss with me

430
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:13,000
coincide perfectly.

431
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:17,400
Do you really think so?

432
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:18,000
Yes.

433
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:19,240
I really think so.

434
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,240
You're not here to plead for him?

435
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:25,120
Does this count as pleading?

436
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,320
I thought I was just sharing

437
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:29,440
my thoughts with my mentor.

438
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:31,480
Understood.

439
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:32,920
Guo Zijian

440
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:36,440
is currently a pot of half-cooked porridge.

441
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:38,840
He still needs a slow fire

442
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:40,680
to simmer him properly.

443
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:45,600
Grandpa, Grandma.

444
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:47,480
Xiaoshan is here.

445
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:48,160
Come, come, come.

446
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:48,760
Watching TV?

447
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:49,280
Have a seat, have a seat.

448
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,120
I missed you so much.

449
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:54,000
I missed you too, Grandma.

450
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:56,640
Where's my brother?

451
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:58,160
As soon as he got back,

452
00:22:58,160 --> 00:23:00,640
he holed up in his room and hasn't come out.

453
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:03,280
I don't know what's wrong with him.

454
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:05,720
What else could it be?

455
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:08,120
He had another fight with my dad.

456
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,600
Another fight?

457
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:12,720
What was it about this time?

458
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:14,040
Chen Xiaoshan.

459
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:14,800
Here!

460
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:15,600
Come in.

461
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:27,400
I'm warning you.

462
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:30,360
Don't say a word to Grandma and Grandpa about today.

463
00:23:30,840 --> 00:23:31,600
About what?

464
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:33,120
About my discharge.

465
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:37,600
I promise I won't blab this time.

466
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:40,440
You've lost all credibility with me.

467
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:42,640
I was just trying to get you two to make up.

468
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:44,240
Then don't waste your time.

469
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:45,240
Let me tell you,

470
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:47,320
Dad and I will never make up.

471
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:48,920
Bro.

472
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:49,400
Enough.

473
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:52,080
Don't plead for him.

474
00:23:52,520 --> 00:23:53,240
It's no use.

475
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:57,080
You really are Dad's son.

476
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:58,920
You say the exact same things.

477
00:23:59,040 --> 00:24:00,280
And have the same awful temper.

478
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:05,120
Xiao Xu, it's me.

479
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:07,480
I remember you telling me

480
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:08,560
that your cousin

481
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:10,120
is in the same unit as our Zijian.

482
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:13,680
Could you please ask him

483
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:15,600
how Zijian has been doing lately?

484
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:18,360
Nothing's wrong.

485
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:20,080
It's just that his dad misses him.

486
00:24:20,080 --> 00:24:21,400
They haven't seen each other in a while,

487
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:22,560
and he's quite worried about him.

488
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:26,680
Okay, sorry to trouble you.

489
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:28,840
Okay, bye.

490
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:30,840
Who were you calling?

491
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:33,000
Our Head Nurse Xu has a patient's case

492
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:33,920
that I needed to discuss with her.

493
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:43,800
Aren't you getting discharged?

494
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:44,960
Why are you still reading this?

495
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:45,960
It's a habit.

496
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:47,320
I read in a book that

497
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:49,880
it takes 21 days to form a habit.

498
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:51,600
If you don't like being a soldier,

499
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:52,760
it won't even take a month back home

500
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:53,280
for you to

501
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:55,040
fully adapt to a new lifestyle.

502
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,320
Leaving the army

503
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:58,480
isn't as simple as breaking a habit.

504
00:24:58,720 --> 00:24:59,960
You wouldn't understand.

505
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:03,000
Bro.

506
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:05,320
I think you really like the army.

507
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:08,800
I can actually start my business alone.

508
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:10,400
You don't need to do this for me.

509
00:25:12,800 --> 00:25:14,120
You really are overthinking it.

510
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:16,320
Then why are you getting discharged?

511
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:19,680
Didn't you say you were going on a mission last time we talked?

512
00:25:20,280 --> 00:25:22,000
The mission didn't go well. We lost.

513
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:23,520
What do you know?

514
00:25:23,760 --> 00:25:24,840
How would I not know?

515
00:25:24,840 --> 00:25:26,440
Our family is in the military supply business.

516
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,920
You think I don't know what a mission means?

517
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:31,360
But a loss is a loss.

518
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:33,960
You can't always win in life, right?

519
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:36,160
But some people

520
00:25:37,120 --> 00:25:38,720
lost their entire lives to it.

521
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:40,880
Who?

522
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:47,160
Enough. Hurry back.

523
00:25:50,200 --> 00:25:50,680
By the way,

524
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,520
you haven't said what you needed Mom for.

525
00:25:53,800 --> 00:25:54,440
Chen Xiaoshan,

526
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:56,960
you only get one chance to make up for your mistake.

527
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:57,840
Tell me first,

528
00:25:58,120 --> 00:25:59,280
can you complete the mission?

529
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:02,040
I guarantee I'll complete it.

530
00:26:06,840 --> 00:26:09,320
Your brother wanted me to look into prosthetics for his comrade.

531
00:26:10,400 --> 00:26:11,000
Right.

532
00:26:16,120 --> 00:26:16,640
Mom,

533
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:19,520
send me his comrade's details.

534
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:20,920
I'll go ask for him tomorrow.

535
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:21,560
Okay.

536
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:25,600
We can't let Dad know about this.

537
00:26:25,600 --> 00:26:27,720
You know his awful temper.

538
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:29,400
Your dad

539
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:31,960
just talks tough,

540
00:26:32,080 --> 00:26:33,160
but deep down,

541
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:34,680
he really cares about your brother.

542
00:26:58,480 --> 00:26:59,280
Dad.

543
00:26:59,560 --> 00:27:01,920
Can I be a soldier when I grow up?

544
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:03,920
Of course. Come here.

545
00:27:09,760 --> 00:27:10,600
Are you happy?

546
00:27:10,680 --> 00:27:13,360
In a second, we'll look at the camera.

547
00:27:14,360 --> 00:27:16,080
Our Zijian is so handsome.

548
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:16,920
One day,

549
00:27:16,920 --> 00:27:18,680
you'll be an even better soldier than Dad.

550
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:19,680
Come on, look here.

551
00:27:21,960 --> 00:27:24,000
Ready, three, two, one.

552
00:27:46,760 --> 00:27:47,320
Son.

553
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,040
Let's talk.

554
00:27:50,200 --> 00:27:51,760
I have nothing to say to you.

555
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:03,520
Your stamina is way worse than mine when I was young.

556
00:28:03,680 --> 00:28:04,760
I'm telling you,

557
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:06,800
you didn't train properly in the army, did you?

558
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:08,600
Just slacking off.

559
00:28:09,440 --> 00:28:11,280
Stop right there! Stop!

560
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:22,160
What's wrong?

561
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,360
Is tricking me fun for you?

562
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:28,280
All's fair in war.

563
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:29,280
It's called tactics.

564
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:32,880
I think you're the one out of shape.

565
00:28:33,120 --> 00:28:34,960
Eating rich food every day as a boss,

566
00:28:35,360 --> 00:28:36,800
you've long forgotten your military training.

567
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:38,720
Cut the nonsense.

568
00:28:39,320 --> 00:28:40,360
Give it to me straight.

569
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:42,440
Do you want to leave the army that badly?

570
00:28:42,880 --> 00:28:44,960
After so many years of military service,

571
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:46,520
do you feel no attachment at all?

572
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:51,520
What's wrong with being a soldier?

573
00:28:52,520 --> 00:28:53,680
In our family, your grandfather,

574
00:28:54,040 --> 00:28:55,200
me, and you.

575
00:28:55,320 --> 00:28:56,720
Three generations of soldiers.

576
00:28:57,040 --> 00:28:58,960
Back then, if it weren't to answer

577
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:00,360
the military's call,

578
00:29:00,640 --> 00:29:02,960
to make room for educated youths,

579
00:29:03,280 --> 00:29:04,520
even if you beat me to death,

580
00:29:04,760 --> 00:29:06,200
I never would've left the army.

581
00:29:06,280 --> 00:29:07,240
But look at you.

582
00:29:07,360 --> 00:29:08,760
The military's conditions are so good now,

583
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:11,400
yet you want to leave.

584
00:29:11,480 --> 00:29:13,200
You're ruining our family's tradition.

585
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:15,160
You're destroying the military spirit.

586
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:16,920
If your mother were alive,

587
00:29:17,480 --> 00:29:19,320
she'd never agree to this.

588
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:20,720
Don't you dare mention my mom.

589
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:21,880
What right do you have?

590
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:23,920
Did you ever care about her? Or me?

591
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:26,360
Bringing up tradition and military spirit?

592
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:27,600
You're not worthy.

593
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:30,280
Stop right there!

594
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:31,120
Stop right...

595
00:29:47,200 --> 00:29:47,920
Grandpa,

596
00:29:50,240 --> 00:29:51,040
better head home.

597
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:52,880
Your grandma

598
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:54,720
is waiting for breakfast.

599
00:30:06,880 --> 00:30:07,440
Huzi,

600
00:30:08,240 --> 00:30:09,440
you don't have to keep coming over.

601
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:10,840
There are nurses here.

602
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:12,480
It's fine, Squad Leader.

603
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:13,480
As long as I'm not busy,

604
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:14,320
I'll come keep you company.

605
00:30:17,520 --> 00:30:20,680
I heard they're reviewing the lessons from the exercise.

606
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:21,680
What did they say?

607
00:30:21,920 --> 00:30:23,040
Tell me about it.

608
00:30:24,800 --> 00:30:26,000
It's all good.

609
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:32,920
Huzi.

610
00:30:33,560 --> 00:30:34,760
You're not yourself today.

611
00:30:35,240 --> 00:30:36,440
Nothing's wrong, Squad Leader.

612
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:38,520
Don't think just because I'm missing a leg now

613
00:30:38,560 --> 00:30:39,680
that I can't kick you.

614
00:30:43,760 --> 00:30:44,360
Lin Yihu!

615
00:30:45,800 --> 00:30:46,320
Here!

616
00:30:47,560 --> 00:30:49,240
Did something happen to the Battalion Commander?

617
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:51,120
Squad Leader...

618
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:53,120
The Battalion Commander...

619
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:57,480
He's already left.

620
00:31:07,320 --> 00:31:09,320
Guo Zijian caused such a huge mess,

621
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:10,720
and all he gets is a vacation?

622
00:31:11,080 --> 00:31:12,600
Then what happens after his vacation?

623
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:15,920
What kind of conclusion is that?

624
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:18,720
Regarding his disciplinary action,

625
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:20,520
the Party Committee is currently divided.

626
00:31:20,560 --> 00:31:22,640
What's there to be divided about?

627
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:24,760
He actually made a scene at the committee meeting!

628
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:27,280
Who does he think he is? The Monkey King?

629
00:31:28,200 --> 00:31:29,080
Now this whole incident

630
00:31:29,080 --> 00:31:31,040
within the Group Army and Theater Command Army headquarters

631
00:31:31,040 --> 00:31:32,920
has spread to every level.

632
00:31:34,240 --> 00:31:36,000
Why don't you make the decision for the committee?

633
00:31:36,120 --> 00:31:36,800
It's not that.

634
00:31:39,320 --> 00:31:42,080
Your promotion is at a critical juncture right now.

635
00:31:42,080 --> 00:31:43,200
That's a separate matter.

636
00:31:43,200 --> 00:31:43,760
Report!

637
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:45,440
Come in.

638
00:31:49,440 --> 00:31:50,080
What is it?

639
00:31:50,400 --> 00:31:50,840
Sir,

640
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:54,160
there's a veteran named Wu Dongsheng downstairs to see you.

641
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:55,760
Wu Dongsheng?

642
00:32:09,080 --> 00:32:09,840
Wu Dongsheng.

643
00:32:10,960 --> 00:32:12,000
Why are you back?

644
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:14,720
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

645
00:32:15,280 --> 00:32:16,840
Your injury hasn't healed yet.

646
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:17,360
Come, come, come.

647
00:32:17,760 --> 00:32:18,280
Sit here.

648
00:32:18,320 --> 00:32:19,640
Take it easy, take it easy.

649
00:32:21,520 --> 00:32:22,080
Come, come.

650
00:32:22,080 --> 00:32:23,080
Do you have a death wish?

651
00:32:23,800 --> 00:32:24,720
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

652
00:32:25,160 --> 00:32:26,360
My injury is fine.

653
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:29,200
I don't want any credit.

654
00:32:29,640 --> 00:32:31,080
Please let our battalion commander come back.

655
00:32:32,480 --> 00:32:33,320
Squad Leader Wu.

656
00:32:33,800 --> 00:32:35,120
The issue with Guo Zijian

657
00:32:35,320 --> 00:32:36,880
isn't about requesting a merit for you.

658
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:44,120
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

659
00:32:45,560 --> 00:32:46,880
I came here today

660
00:32:47,600 --> 00:32:48,880
just to tell you

661
00:32:49,520 --> 00:32:51,480
my injury has nothing to do with the battalion commander.

662
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:53,200
Back then,

663
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:55,120
I was the one who volunteered

664
00:32:55,120 --> 00:32:56,440
to scout Huangshi Ridge.

665
00:32:57,840 --> 00:32:58,360
Squad Leader Wu,

666
00:32:59,280 --> 00:33:00,400
we all know

667
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:02,120
you don't want to lose your battalion commander.

668
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:04,800
But you can't absolve him

669
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:05,560
by telling lies.

670
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:07,920
I'm not telling lies.

671
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:08,720
Calm down, calm down.

672
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:09,440
Take your time.

673
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,560
Everything I said is true.

674
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,720
If you don't believe me, ask Lin Yihu.

675
00:33:16,920 --> 00:33:18,520
Ask the comrades in the recon squad.

676
00:33:20,720 --> 00:33:22,200
Before the battalion commander gave the order,

677
00:33:23,080 --> 00:33:24,440
I was already prepared

678
00:33:24,920 --> 00:33:26,080
to volunteer for the mission.

679
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:27,320
So,

680
00:33:28,200 --> 00:33:29,320
if someone must be punished,

681
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:31,640
then punish me.

682
00:33:32,960 --> 00:33:34,720
But he is the commander of the 1st Battalion.

683
00:33:35,840 --> 00:33:37,160
Not only did he violate discipline

684
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:39,680
and cause a major error during the drill,

685
00:33:40,040 --> 00:33:42,480
but he also caused a serious accident.

686
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:45,240
These are responsibilities he must bear.

687
00:33:45,320 --> 00:33:47,480
Battalion Commander Guo didn't intentionally disobey orders.

688
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:51,080
He just genuinely wanted to win this battle.

689
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:53,920
I know.

690
00:33:56,080 --> 00:33:57,720
I'm just a squad leader.

691
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:01,960
I have no right to plead for him in front of you.

692
00:34:03,720 --> 00:34:05,240
But speaking from the heart,

693
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:09,159
before Battalion Commander Guo came to the 1st Battalion,

694
00:34:09,840 --> 00:34:11,320
you know what state the 1st Battalion was in.

695
00:34:13,080 --> 00:34:14,520
Now that finally

696
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:16,840
everyone's morale is up,

697
00:34:17,520 --> 00:34:18,840
and we want to train hard

698
00:34:18,840 --> 00:34:20,480
and fight well.

699
00:34:22,080 --> 00:34:23,440
We can't just

700
00:34:23,600 --> 00:34:26,080
let it fall apart so easily.

701
00:34:27,199 --> 00:34:27,960
Wu.

702
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:33,480
I understand how you feel.

703
00:34:35,719 --> 00:34:36,920
Regarding his issue,

704
00:34:37,440 --> 00:34:38,880
the Party committee is meeting to discuss it.

705
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:40,840
I assure you

706
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:43,080
I will pass on your opinions

707
00:34:43,159 --> 00:34:45,480
to every member of the leadership team.

708
00:34:45,880 --> 00:34:46,639
Alright?

709
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:50,920
But our military has its discipline

710
00:34:51,560 --> 00:34:52,679
and its regulations.

711
00:34:54,199 --> 00:34:55,400
As for exactly how it's handled,

712
00:34:57,120 --> 00:34:59,000
it's not up to me alone.

713
00:35:00,760 --> 00:35:02,080
As for your personal issue,

714
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:04,160
don't worry.

715
00:35:05,680 --> 00:35:06,200
Wu,

716
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:09,160
we won't ignore it.

717
00:35:09,880 --> 00:35:10,640
Remember,

718
00:35:11,080 --> 00:35:12,280
the top priority

719
00:35:12,800 --> 00:35:14,200
is for you to recover from your injury.

720
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:16,200
Understood?

721
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:17,640
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

722
00:35:18,760 --> 00:35:20,400
I understand everything you said.

723
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:23,280
As for my issue,

724
00:35:24,120 --> 00:35:25,720
I really don't need to trouble the unit.

725
00:35:27,920 --> 00:35:28,680
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

726
00:35:32,160 --> 00:35:33,400
I came here today

727
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:35,520
for no other reason.

728
00:35:37,720 --> 00:35:39,240
Just as a veteran,

729
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:43,600
I want to beg the brigade leaders

730
00:35:44,760 --> 00:35:46,000
for the sake of our 1st Battalion,

731
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:49,040
for the sake of our unit,

732
00:35:51,880 --> 00:35:54,160
to keep a good battalion commander.

733
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:53,640
Why do you have to butt heads with him?

734
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:56,440
Alright.

735
00:37:00,320 --> 00:37:02,520
That's much better. Much better.

736
00:37:02,600 --> 00:37:03,160
Director Qi,

737
00:37:03,600 --> 00:37:05,440
about the patient's condition you mentioned,

738
00:37:05,480 --> 00:37:06,400
we've looked into it.

739
00:37:07,120 --> 00:37:08,000
Mr. Chen is here too.

740
00:37:08,240 --> 00:37:08,760
Perfect timing.

741
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:12,040
Didn't Junmeng Group independently develop a

742
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:13,120
smart prosthesis?

743
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:15,720
I think it perfectly suits his condition.

744
00:37:15,720 --> 00:37:16,440
Let me see.

745
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:21,960
Wu Dongsheng.

746
00:37:22,440 --> 00:37:23,800
This is Zijian's comrade.

747
00:37:24,080 --> 00:37:25,960
Zijian came back this time for him.

748
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:27,720
He deliberately mentioned leaving the military

749
00:37:27,920 --> 00:37:29,280
just to spite you.

750
00:37:29,400 --> 00:37:31,520
Why can't you just talk to him nicely?

751
00:37:31,920 --> 00:37:33,880
You're like a firecracker, going off instantly.

752
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:35,680
I'm not the one going off instantly.

753
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:37,480
He can talk nicely to all of you,

754
00:37:37,480 --> 00:37:38,600
but not me.

755
00:37:39,240 --> 00:37:40,560
He's always giving me

756
00:37:40,560 --> 00:37:41,560
an attitude.

757
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:44,880
Doesn't he need a prosthesis?

758
00:37:45,640 --> 00:37:46,800
Have him come talk to me.

759
00:37:49,880 --> 00:37:50,880
Not this again.

760
00:37:52,040 --> 00:37:53,960
He just wants me to compromise.

761
00:37:54,280 --> 00:37:54,920
I know.

762
00:37:55,840 --> 00:37:56,880
Zijian.

763
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:58,880
He's your own father.

764
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:00,920
For the sake of your comrade,

765
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:02,960
what does compromising matter?

766
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:08,440
Fine.

767
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:10,640
Then I'll go talk to him.

768
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:16,360
How did your comrade injure his leg?

769
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:18,160
An exercise accident.

770
00:38:18,840 --> 00:38:19,720
It has nothing to do with you.

771
00:38:21,640 --> 00:38:23,560
Is this your attitude when asking for help?

772
00:38:25,320 --> 00:38:26,160
What do you want, then?

773
00:38:26,960 --> 00:38:28,600
I can add your comrade

774
00:38:29,160 --> 00:38:31,080
to the trial list,

775
00:38:31,360 --> 00:38:33,400
but you must agree to one condition.

776
00:38:33,640 --> 00:38:34,120
Okay.

777
00:38:34,880 --> 00:38:36,040
Any condition is fine.

778
00:38:36,360 --> 00:38:37,800
I'd even trade my own leg.

779
00:38:38,040 --> 00:38:39,240
What would I want your leg for?

780
00:38:39,960 --> 00:38:40,640
To make ham?

781
00:38:43,360 --> 00:38:44,400
Tomorrow,

782
00:38:44,400 --> 00:38:46,800
I'm hosting a dinner for my old comrades.

783
00:38:46,880 --> 00:38:48,960
You're in charge of arranging it for me.

784
00:38:49,560 --> 00:38:50,320
That's it?

785
00:38:50,400 --> 00:38:51,000
That's it.

786
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:53,200
Tomorrow morning at nine,

787
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:54,800
report here on time.

788
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:56,720
Alright.

789
00:38:58,200 --> 00:38:59,000
Wait.

790
00:39:02,800 --> 00:39:04,880
It's noon. Let's have lunch together.

791
00:39:05,600 --> 00:39:06,120
I'll pass.

792
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:21,000
What's this for?

793
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:22,520
You forgot?

794
00:39:22,520 --> 00:39:24,120
Xiaohui's birthday gift.

795
00:39:24,720 --> 00:39:25,960
You forgot your own son's birthday?

796
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:27,840
Last time, you said

797
00:39:27,840 --> 00:39:29,880
you'd take him to the zoo to see tigers on his birthday.

798
00:39:35,040 --> 00:39:35,880
Did I say that?

799
00:39:36,600 --> 00:39:37,680
Hurry up.

800
00:39:38,520 --> 00:39:39,760
Now that we're finally done here,

801
00:39:40,080 --> 00:39:42,640
the instructor and I are on duty this week.

802
00:39:42,880 --> 00:39:44,400
Go spend some time with your wife and kid.

803
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:46,840
Before your wife forgets what you look like.

804
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:50,880
Staff Officer Liang Hong's review summary,

805
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:51,720
you heard it too, right?

806
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:54,840
Do you think

807
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:57,160
her analysis makes sense?

808
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:58,320
Even though

809
00:39:58,320 --> 00:40:00,200
Guo Zijian's strike on the Blue Force command post

810
00:40:00,200 --> 00:40:01,480
was ruled invalid,

811
00:40:02,160 --> 00:40:02,880
the fact that

812
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:05,240
he could, in that situation,

813
00:40:05,680 --> 00:40:07,960
accurately determine the Blue Force command post's

814
00:40:07,960 --> 00:40:08,760
exact location...

815
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:10,320
shows real skill.

816
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:12,040
But it is exactly for this reason

817
00:40:12,240 --> 00:40:13,880
that he became overconfident,

818
00:40:14,080 --> 00:40:16,720
choosing to attack Tiger Mouth instead of falling back.

819
00:40:17,160 --> 00:40:17,640
Right.

820
00:40:18,600 --> 00:40:20,920
That is what ultimately caused our defeat.

821
00:40:21,080 --> 00:40:21,760
Exactly.

822
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:26,160
The battle at Yuhuang Peak

823
00:40:27,200 --> 00:40:28,440
was clearly a trap

824
00:40:28,480 --> 00:40:29,960
set for us by Long Yuanshan.

825
00:40:30,840 --> 00:40:31,960
Then let's think about this.

826
00:40:32,440 --> 00:40:33,400
If Guo Zijian

827
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:35,240
had given up on Tiger Mouth

828
00:40:35,440 --> 00:40:36,680
and chosen to fall back,

829
00:40:37,680 --> 00:40:38,520
the outcome...

830
00:40:39,360 --> 00:40:40,440
how much could it have changed?

831
00:40:41,480 --> 00:40:42,280
Hard to say.

832
00:40:42,960 --> 00:40:45,040
If it were you, what would you choose?

833
00:40:47,720 --> 00:40:48,760
If it were me,

834
00:40:49,880 --> 00:40:51,600
I would also choose to go to Tiger Mouth.

835
00:40:52,360 --> 00:40:53,000
No.

836
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:56,680
You wouldn't.

837
00:40:58,440 --> 00:40:59,160
Neither would I.

838
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:04,120
Because neither of us is Guo Zijian.

839
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:07,440
Yeah.

840
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:09,800
Guo Zijian

841
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:12,040
is like a fierce tiger.

842
00:41:13,160 --> 00:41:14,640
The usual rules and regulations

843
00:41:15,240 --> 00:41:16,480
can't hold him back.

844
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:21,440
Guo Zijian, oh, Guo Zijian...

845
00:41:21,680 --> 00:41:23,760
Without a fierce tiger like you,

846
00:41:24,960 --> 00:41:26,120
what are we supposed to do?

847
00:41:40,160 --> 00:41:41,040
Staff Officer Liang.

848
00:41:44,480 --> 00:41:45,440
Commander Jiang.

849
00:41:48,040 --> 00:41:48,720
Staff Officer Liang.

850
00:41:48,800 --> 00:41:49,320
Commander Jiang.

851
00:41:53,360 --> 00:41:55,280
Welcome. A warm welcome.

852
00:41:55,400 --> 00:41:56,880
Welcome to our brigade, Staff Officer Liang,

853
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:58,800
to share insights and lessons from the exercise.

854
00:41:59,040 --> 00:41:59,920
Thank you, thank you so much.

855
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:01,280
You're too kind.

856
00:42:01,320 --> 00:42:02,360
Say, Staff Officer Liang,

857
00:42:02,360 --> 00:42:03,480
I'm a straight shooter,

858
00:42:03,640 --> 00:42:04,520
so please bear with me.

859
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:05,720
What I mean is,

860
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:07,720
you shouldn't play favorites.

861
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:08,640
Right?

862
00:42:08,880 --> 00:42:11,520
You can't just share insights with the 1st Battalion.

863
00:42:11,600 --> 00:42:12,200
Our 2nd Battalion

864
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:14,400
also has a lot of questions for you.

865
00:42:14,920 --> 00:42:16,040
Commander Jiang, you've misunderstood.

866
00:42:16,080 --> 00:42:17,120
I'm not playing favorites.

867
00:42:17,560 --> 00:42:19,520
I was the evaluator for the 1st Battalion in this exercise,

868
00:42:19,520 --> 00:42:20,800
so I know about their situation

869
00:42:20,800 --> 00:42:22,080
in much greater detail.

870
00:42:22,320 --> 00:42:23,560
The commanders asked me to focus

871
00:42:23,560 --> 00:42:24,680
on the 1st Battalion.

872
00:42:25,120 --> 00:42:26,520
Yes, I understand.

873
00:42:27,440 --> 00:42:28,640
But having said that,

874
00:42:29,160 --> 00:42:31,120
the 1st Battalion's experiences and lessons

875
00:42:31,240 --> 00:42:32,640
for our 2nd Battalion,

876
00:42:33,080 --> 00:42:35,320
are also highly valuable references.

877
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:36,440
Wouldn't you agree?

878
00:42:37,200 --> 00:42:38,840
So I think...

879
00:42:38,960 --> 00:42:39,920
How about this?

880
00:42:39,920 --> 00:42:41,840
Could you give our 2nd Battalion some special treatment

881
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:43,320
and give us a private session?

882
00:42:43,400 --> 00:42:44,360
Sure, no problem.

883
00:42:44,640 --> 00:42:45,120
This way, please.

884
00:42:45,400 --> 00:42:46,360
The 2nd Battalion is over here.

885
00:42:46,440 --> 00:42:47,040
Right now?

886
00:42:47,040 --> 00:42:47,560
Right now.

887
00:42:50,520 --> 00:42:51,320
All right, let's go.

888
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:51,800
After you.
